{
  "_about": "Component spec for pos-breadcrumb (built 2026-09-19 from an inspiration screenshot and a responsive-behavior requirement). Single source of truth for the Variants/Usage/Tokens tabs on /style-guide. Two variants: 'expanded' (all items visible, chevron-separated) and 'collapsed' (only the current item shown, plus a back-chevron button that opens a popover listing the hidden ancestor links) — the real component switches between them automatically via a ResizeObserver in assets/js/pos-breadcrumb.js when the list overflows its container; the docs preview's Variant toggle applies the same .pos-breadcrumb--collapsed class manually to demo the result. Reuses .pos-link (ancestor links) and .pos-popover + the native HTML popover API (collapsed-state flyout) rather than duplicating their styling or tokens — per the composedOf field and the real, confirmed repo convention (checked multiselect.json/dialog.json), a composed component's own nested-component tokens are not repeated here, they belong to that component's own spec page. Regenerate spec-breadcrumb.liquid via scripts/generate-component.js (or the inline regen snippet in RULES.md §6.4) after any change here — never hand-edit the .liquid partial. 2026-10-06: the collapsed flyout's parent-page links use --pos-color-interactive-text (Figma: Interactive text normal), not the generic popover menu's grey.",
  "component": "breadcrumb",
  "name": "Breadcrumb",
  "description": "A horizontal trail of links showing the current page's location within a nested hierarchy, with a chevron separator between items and the current page shown as plain (non-link) text. Collapses to a back-chevron + current item when it doesn't fit its container.",
  "whenToUse": [
    "Showing the user's location within a nested page hierarchy (e.g. Category > Subcategory > Product).",
    "Letting the user jump back up to any ancestor page in one click.",
    "The hierarchy has at least two levels above the current page."
  ],
  "whenNotToUse": [
    "Navigation is flat/single-level — a breadcrumb with only the current page adds no value.",
    "The full path would be longer and more confusing to scan than the page's own title or a back button."
  ],
  "do": [
    "Keep each label short and match the real title of the page it links to.",
    "Always show the current page last, as plain non-link text.",
    "Let the component collapse automatically when it doesn't fit its container — never truncate labels with CSS ellipsis instead."
  ],
  "dont": [
    "Make the current page a clickable link — it isn't navigable to itself.",
    "Use a breadcrumb as the only way to reach a page — it supplements primary navigation, it doesn't replace it.",
    "Invent labels that differ from the actual page titles in the hierarchy."
  ],
  "accessibility": [
    "The root element is a <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"> so assistive tech announces it as a distinct landmark.",
    "The current page uses aria-current=\"page\", not a visual-only style.",
    "Separator icons are aria-hidden — they're purely decorative, the list structure itself conveys order.",
    "The collapsed-state back button has a real aria-label (e.g. \"Show parent pages\") since its icon alone conveys no accessible name."
  ],
  "composedOf": [
    "link",
    "popover"
  ],
  "props": [
    {
      "name": "items",
      "type": "list of {label, href}",
      "default": "none",
      "description": "The ordered list of ancestor pages plus the current page, rendered as <li> entries inside the breadcrumb's <ol>. The same list also populates the collapsed-state popover menu."
    }
  ],
  "dimensions": {
    "variant": [
      "expanded",
      "collapsed"
    ],
    "state": [
      "normal",
      "hover",
      "focus"
    ]
  },
